---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /blog.html
title: Blog
description: Writing from the EISS network on European security studies, including work by our volunteers and interns published under their own names.
lang: en
---
{# The blog index (#1259). English only, and the page says so rather than
   implying a translation is coming: rule §1 forbids machine translation, so
   every locale added here is a hand-translation burden on every future post,
   forever. The chrome is not localised for the same reason.

   Posts come from the `blog` tag, set for the whole directory in
   src/blog/blog.11tydata.js, so publishing needs no edit to this file. #}
{% from "icons.njk" import icon %}

<header class="page-header">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Blog</span>
    <h1>Blog</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">
      Writing from the network on European security studies. Volunteers and interns publish here
      under their own names, drawing on the
      <a href="/anthology.html">Anthology</a>, which puts nine editions of conference papers behind
      a piece before its author writes a word.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: var(--space-4);">
      <a class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" href="/feed.xml">{{ icon("rss") }} Subscribe by feed</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    {%- set posts = collections.blog | reverse %}
    {%- if posts.length %}
    <ul class="blog-list">
      {%- for post in posts %}
      <li class="blog-item">
        <time class="blog-date" datetime="{{ post.date.toISOString().slice(0, 10) }}">
          {{ post.date.toISOString() | newsDate("en") }}
        </time>
        <h2 class="blog-item-title"><a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a></h2>
        <p class="blog-item-byline">
          {{ post.data.author }}{% if post.data.authorNote %}, {{ post.data.authorNote }}{% endif %}
        </p>
        {%- if post.data.summary %}<p class="blog-summary">{{ post.data.summary }}</p>{% endif %}
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    {%- else %}
    <p class="muted">No posts yet.</p>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-tight">
  <div class="container">
    <article class="card" style="padding: clamp(var(--space-6), 2vw + 1rem, var(--space-8));">
      <div class="prose" style="margin-inline: 0;">
        <h2>Writing for us</h2>
        <p>
          Volunteers and interns are offered a piece here as a defined part of their placement, not
          as something we fit in at the end. If that is why you are reading this, the
          <a href="/internship.html">volunteering page</a> covers how a placement works.
        </p>
        <p>
          Posts are read before they go up and we may decide not to publish one. Anything here
          carries the EISS name and a permanent address, so it cannot be quietly withdrawn later.
          That decision is a judgement about a text and nothing else.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>The blog is in English only.</strong> The rest of the site is translated into
          French and German by hand, and we do not machine-translate anything. Committing to three
          languages for every post would mean fewer posts rather than more readers, so we would
          rather publish and say plainly that this part of the site is not translated.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
